<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.186 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.186 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$3.5 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due June 26 was 3.186 percent, up from 3.088 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.6 billion of 182-day T-bills due September 25, 1997 was 3.479 percent, up from 3.418 percent last week, and on C$1.1 billion of 357-day T-bills due March 19, 1998 was 3.918 percent, up from 3.900 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$600 million three-month, C$150 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$600 million of C$8.0 billion bills due April 3.</p>
